# Normalize every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# GitHub stores exactly the bytes that are committed — it does not convert line
# endings on push or on display. Without this, a file first committed from a
# CRLF editor keeps CRLF forever, and any later tool-driven edit rewrites the
# whole file to LF: a one-line change then arrives as a diff touching every
# line, burying the real edit and destroying `git blame` for that file. That is
# exactly what happened to assets/js/usage.js.
#
# `eol=lf` also matters for scripts/*.sh: a CRLF shebang line makes the kernel
# look for an interpreter with a trailing carriage return and fail.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files, never converted. `text=auto` already detects each of these by
# content, but declaring them means a heuristic miss can never corrupt one —
# and the i18n .mo catalogs are compiled gettext output where a single
# substituted byte silently breaks translations at runtime.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.mo   binary

# Yarn's vendored runtime: keep it out of language stats and out of diffs.
/.yarn/**            linguist-vendored
/.yarn/releases/*    binary
/.yarn/plugins/**/*  binary
/.pnp.*              binary linguist-generated
